Simple Mods Manager - License
=============================

Copyright (c) 2026 undefined418. All rights reserved.

This license covers everything in this repository - the Simple Mods Manager
engine and UI, the SMM Loader (loader/), the SMM Handler (handler/), the
documentation and the build tooling - except bundled third-party components,
which keep their own licenses.


1. What you may do today
------------------------

You may use Simple Mods Manager for personal, non-commercial purposes through
the official releases, which are published at https://github.com/0x78f1935/SMM
and are free to download and use. All other rights are reserved. In
particular, you may not read the source code or build it, redistribute the
source code or binaries built from it, publish modified versions, or reuse
any part of the code in other projects.


2. The community purchase pledge
--------------------------------

When cumulative community support through Buy Me a Coffee
(https://buymeacoffee.com/undefined418) reaches EUR 75,000, the author will
relicense this entire repository under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 (GPLv3) - permanently and irrevocably. In plain words: the
community collectively buys the source code, and once bought, it belongs to
everyone.

EUR 75,000 is simply the price the author will sell it for. What that buys,
counted rather than estimated: roughly 49,000 lines of Python across 98
engine modules, an original native loader and an original
ScriptHookV-compatible script handler (the SMM Handler) together comprising
roughly 26,000 lines of C++, roughly 10,500 lines of UI code,
2,475 automated tests, and capabilities no other public tool ships
(Legacy-to-Enhanced conversion of models, textures and vehicle fragments,
OIV-to-SML package translation, the original loader and script handler
themselves). Every one of those figures is checkable in the repository
once it is yours.

GPLv3 is chosen deliberately: its copyleft means that once the community has
bought the code, nobody can take a fork closed-source and resell the work -
it stays open for everyone who paid for it, and everyone after them.


